# About Clearfield, Inc.

Clearfield, Inc. (Nasdaq: CLFD) designs, manufactures and distributes fiber optic equipment — the FieldSmart® product line — for faster, easier deployment of fiber to the premises (FTTP/FTTH). Our solutions are built for today's high-bandwidth requirements and designed to help network operators quickly launch, scale and adapt fiber networks.

## Who We Are

We're a publicly traded company (Nasdaq: CLFD) based in Brooklyn Park, Minnesota — a suburb of Minneapolis. We design, manufacture and distribute fiber optic physical layer components and systems — the "connective tissue" of fiber networks.

**Products include:**
- Fiber management and connectivity products
- Fiber distribution hubs (FDH)
- Drop cable and pre-connectorized solutions
- Fiber wall outlets, OSP and ISP products
- WaveReady DWDM solutions

**Markets served:**
- Broadband service providers (ISPs, telcos, cable MSOs)
- Municipalities and cooperatives
- Government and utility networks

## Our Mission

To simplify, scale and deploy fiber faster and more efficiently.

## Company Size

Approximately 600 employees as of 2024, following workforce reductions due to market normalization post-BEAD delay.

## Financial Snapshot (FY2024)

Revenue was significantly lower than the FY2022 peak ($263M), reflecting post-COVID inventory normalization. Recovery tied to BEAD deployment acceleration.

## Key Differentiators

- Domestic manufacturing (Brooklyn Park, MN)
- Rapid deployment architecture (pre-connectorized, plug-and-play)
- Focus on outside plant (OSP) fiber management

