# Clearfield Reports Fourth Quarter and Fiscal Year 2024 Results

**BROOKLYN PARK, Minn., November 12, 2024**

Clearfield, Inc. (Nasdaq: CLFD), a manufacturer and distributor of fiber optic equipment, today reported financial results for the fourth quarter and fiscal year ended September 30, 2024.

## Fourth Quarter Fiscal Year 2024 Highlights

- Net revenue: $44.6 million, up 13% sequentially and up 19% year-over-year
- Gross margin: 41.2%
- Net income: $2.1 million, or $0.10 per diluted share

## Full Fiscal Year 2024 Highlights

- Net revenue: $153.3 million, down from $263.1 million in fiscal year 2022
- Recovery underway as inventory normalization completes and BEAD deployments begin

## Management Commentary

"We are encouraged by the sequential improvement in revenue in the second half of fiscal 2024 as our customers work through their inventory positions and begin to ramp for BEAD-funded deployments," said Cheri Beranek, President and CEO. "We believe fiscal 2025 and beyond represent a return to growth as BEAD deployments accelerate and operators begin spending again."

## Business Context

Clearfield sells primarily through a two-tier distribution model:
- **Direct sales** to large ISPs, telcos, and cable MSOs
- **Distribution partners** including Anixter/Wesco, Graybar, and other fiber distributors

Key customer types include broadband service providers, rural electric cooperatives, municipalities, and government/utility networks.

