# Clearfield Reports First Quarter Fiscal Year 2025 Results

**BROOKLYN PARK, Minn., January 28, 2025**

Clearfield, Inc. (Nasdaq: CLFD), a manufacturer and distributor of fiber optic equipment, today reported financial results for the first quarter of fiscal year 2025 ended December 31, 2024.

## Q1 FY2025 Highlights

- Net revenue: $47.1 million, up 17% year-over-year
- Gross margin: 43.1%
- Net income: $2.5 million

## Management Commentary

"We are seeing increased order activity from ISPs, rural electric cooperatives, and municipalities as BEAD funding begins to flow and operators move into active procurement mode," said Cheri Beranek, President and CEO. "The pipeline of BEAD-funded projects is substantial, and we expect a meaningful ramp in the second half of calendar 2025 and into 2026."

## Customer Activity

Management noted that smaller and mid-size broadband providers, particularly rural cooperatives and municipal operators, represent the fastest-growing customer segment. These operators are deploying fiber for the first time or significantly expanding existing networks.

## BEAD Context

With BEAD subgrantee agreements being finalized in many states, equipment procurement is expected to accelerate as construction timelines firm up. Clearfield is positioned as a preferred vendor for smaller operators due to its FieldSmart pre-connectorized rapid deployment architecture.

